    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 Caco-2 records classify small basic amines norephedrine and cathine as highly permeable (Papp >1×10^-6 cm/s; norephedrine 10.0×10^-6 cm/s in a mixture), supporting that small ionized primary amines can still be well absorbed; this is analog evidence, not a direct query measurement.",
      "card_ids": ["C38", "C44", "C46"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No L4 record provides affirmative evidence of poor solubility, poor permeability, or F<20% for the query; most L4 records concern unrelated molecules or formulations.",
      "card_ids": ["C36", "C37", "C39", "C40", "C41", "C42", "C43", "C45", "C47"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "intestinal_absorption_permeability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C36", "C37", "C38", "C39", "C40", "C41", "C42", "C43", "C44", "C45", "C46", "C47"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability or matched oral-versus-IV exposure measurement for the query molecule.",
    "No direct permeability or solubility measurement for rimantadine itself; L4 permeability records are for Khat alkaloids, not adamantane amines.",
    "First-pass metabolism of the adamantane primary amine is not directly measured.",
    "Full ionization at pH 7.4 (logD -0.82) leaves some permeability uncertainty, though small size and the lipophilic cage may compensate.",
    "Transfer from record contexts is based on structural analogy, not identical chemistry."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F ≥ 20%) because all visible L1 gold records are positive (≥24%), the most transferable small basic-amine contexts support adequate oral bioavailability, L3 oral-exposure records add supportive but non-quantitative context, and L4 Caco-2 permeability of similar small basic amines supports absorption. No affirmative threshold-relevant low evidence appears; the only sub-20% record is a low-transferability calf result. Confidence remains moderate because no direct query F measurement exists and the query is fully ionized at pH 7.4."
}

